From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 04:55:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 147/225] ASoC: sprd: verify audcp power before codec DP
 register access

An idle "amixer" read of a digital (DP-range) codec control panics with a
fatal async SError: sprd_codec_read/write wrap the DP readl/writel in
agdsp_access_enable(), but that helper takes a fast path (skipping the
wake-mailbox + PMU power-up poll) whenever ap_enable_cnt is already
non-zero, so it can return success while the audcp domain is in
deep-sleep. The subsequent access to the 0x3375xxxx digital window then
async-aborts.

  Kernel panic - Asynchronous SError Interrupt, Comm: amixer
    sprd_codec_read -> codec_digital_reg_disable -> ...

Gate both DP branches on agdsp_can_access(), which reads the PMU
power/sleep status directly (not the refcount). If the core isn't
genuinely powered, skip the access -- read returns 0, write is dropped --
instead of faulting. The playback path is unaffected (its DAPM digital
widget powers audcp and holds it across the stream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
index 2e6d97cc9..69f02e177 100755
--- a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 #include "sprd-asoc-common.h"
 #include "sprd-codec.h"
 #include "sprd-headset.h"
+#include "agdsp_access.h"
 
 #define SOC_REG(r) ((unsigned short)(r))
 #define FUN_REG(f) ((unsigned short)(-((f) + 1)))
@@ -3292,6 +3293,20 @@ static unsigned int sprd_codec_read(struct snd_soc_component *codec,
 			pr_err("%s, agdsp_access_enable failed!\n", __func__);
 			return ret;
 		}
+		/*
+		 * agdsp_access_enable() takes its fast path (skips the wake +
+		 * PMU power-up poll) when ap_enable_cnt is already non-zero, so
+		 * it can return success while the audcp domain is actually in
+		 * deep-sleep -- e.g. an idle amixer read of a DP control. The
+		 * readl below then async-aborts (fatal SError). Confirm the core
+		 * is genuinely powered before touching the digital reg window.
+		 */
+		if (!agdsp_can_access()) {
+			pr_warn_ratelimited("%s: audcp not accessible, DP reg 0x%x read as 0\n",
+					    __func__, reg);
+			agdsp_access_disable();
+			return 0;
+		}
 		codec_digital_reg_enable(codec);
 		ret = readl_relaxed((void __iomem *)(reg -
 			CODEC_DP_BASE + sprd_codec_dp_base));
@@ -3330,6 +3345,13 @@ static int sprd_codec_write(struct snd_soc_component *codec, unsigned int reg,
 			pr_err("%s, agdsp_access_enable failed!\n", __func__);
 			return ret;
 		}
+		/* see sprd_codec_read(): don't touch DP regs if audcp is asleep */
+		if (!agdsp_can_access()) {
+			pr_warn_ratelimited("%s: audcp not accessible, DP reg 0x%x write dropped\n",
+					    __func__, reg);
+			agdsp_access_disable();
+			return 0;
+		}
 		codec_digital_reg_enable(codec);
 		sp_asoc_pr_reg("D[0x%04x] R:[0x%08x]\n",
 			(reg - CODEC_DP_BASE) & 0xFFFF,
